# DISCOVERIES — {{CAMPAIGN_TITLE}}

Settled, multi-evidence findings — the campaign's accumulated knowledge, **positive AND negative**.
Write here ONLY after **(1)** multiple consistent experiments confirm the finding on
`{{PRIMARY_METRIC}}` (with the guardrail behavior noted) **AND (2)** an independent verification
(`{{VERIFY_SKILL}}`) returned CONFIRMED and wrote its verdict artifact — **every entry cites its
`results/verdicts/<id>.json` by name** (the enforcement hook checks the citation). A single good run
is a JOURNAL entry, not a discovery. Number entries D1, D2, ….

**Steering-negatives are discoveries too.** A negative the campaign will *act* on — it kills a
lever/topology branch, declares a ceiling, shelves a direction, or contradicts its a-priori
prediction — is promoted here with its **kill tier** (from the verify verdict): **REFUTED**
(mechanism understood, the idea cannot work → prunes) or **EVIDENCE AGAINST** (clean single negative
→ shelved, revivable; independent entries may accumulate toward a prune). An **INCONCLUSIVE** kill
(cause unattributed — the implementation, not the idea, may be at fault) never graduates: queue a
fix-and-rerun unit instead. Number negative entries N1, N2, … and state the mechanism, not just the
outcome. Routine below-best results stay on the scoreboard.

> **Retractions live HERE, append-only — a reversed finding is never silently deleted or fixed only in a
> side note (a memory file, a later journal line).** When new evidence overturns or narrows a discovery,
> add a dated **`REVISES Dn`** entry *in this file* that states what changed and why, and edit Dn's first
> line to begin `[SUPERSEDED by Dm — see below]` (keep its original text). Also amend the stale claim
> wherever it was copied (the scoreboard row's `notes`/`description`, `{{PHYSICS_DOC}}`). A correction that
> lives only outside DISCOVERIES will be missed by the next agent and the finding rots as "settled."

